WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.067
Thank you. Enjoy yourself. Welcome, everybody.

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:05.067
Welcome, welcome, welcome to "The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:05.067 --> 00:00:07.033
I'm so happy you're here. Thank you for watching.

00:00:07.033 --> 00:00:08.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:11.434
Everyone's in a good mood. This weekend is Halloween.

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:12.701
-Ooh!

00:00:12.701 --> 00:00:14.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:15.567
♪♪

00:00:15.567 --> 00:00:17.033
-I was so touched this morning.

00:00:17.033 --> 00:00:18.767
A kid who lives in my neighborhood

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:20.968
put on a fake patchy beard and said he was going as me.

00:00:20.968 --> 00:00:23.067
Isn't that nice?

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:24.501
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.501 --> 00:00:26.300
I read that this is expected to be

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.467
the biggest Halloween since the pandemic.

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:29.767
Yeah.

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:32.534
[ Cheers and applause ] Yeah. That's right.

00:00:32.534 --> 00:00:34.534
Now that COVID is under control,

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.801
kids can safely return to eating food from strangers.

00:00:36.801 --> 00:00:39.234
That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:39.234 --> 00:00:41.234
People are going all-out.

00:00:41.234 --> 00:00:42.801
I saw that costume spending alone

00:00:42.801 --> 00:00:46.100
projected to hit a record of $3.6 billion.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.901
[ Audience oohs ] 3.6 billion.

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:49.667
To put that in perspective,

00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:52.267
that's almost half as much as Kanye lost this week.

00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:54.367
-Oh. -$3.6 billion.

00:00:54.367 --> 00:00:56.834
A lot of --

00:00:56.834 --> 00:00:59.901
Almost half. [ Laughs ]

00:00:59.901 --> 00:01:01.801
That's right. Halloween is almost here.

00:01:01.801 --> 00:01:03.334
You probably heard a lot of good advice

00:01:03.334 --> 00:01:04.734
about how to safely enjoy the holiday,

00:01:04.734 --> 00:01:05.968
but you have to be on the alert

00:01:05.968 --> 00:01:08.000
because there's a lot of bad advice out there, too.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.767
So, here with some terrible Halloween advice

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:11.667
is our sound engineer, Steve Mandel.

00:01:11.667 --> 00:01:13.167
Steve?

00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:16.501
&gt;&gt; Only trick-or-treat at houses with large dogs.

00:01:16.501 --> 00:01:17.901
If they bite,

00:01:17.901 --> 00:01:20.968
you could be looking at a pretty sweet lawsuit.

00:01:20.968 --> 00:01:22.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.968
-Thank you very much.

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:25.601
Thank you very much, Steve.

00:01:25.601 --> 00:01:27.634
[ Applause ]

00:01:27.634 --> 00:01:29.467
[ Laughter ] Let's get to some news.

00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:31.067
Everybody's talking about this.

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:34.934
Last night, Elon Musk finally closed his deal to buy Twitter.

00:01:34.934 --> 00:01:36.434
[ Audience groans ] Yeah.

00:01:36.434 --> 00:01:39.300
Now he owns SpaceX if he wants to see the heavens,

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.300
and he owns Twitter if he wants to see hell.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.400
[ Laughter ] It's amazing.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:46.567
The first thing Elon did -- this is true -- after taking over

00:01:46.567 --> 00:01:48.467
was fire a bunch of executives.

00:01:48.467 --> 00:01:50.200
Yeah, people said he was cleaning house.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:51.868
Then Elon was like, "I'm a billionaire.

00:01:51.868 --> 00:01:54.567
I don't know what those words mean."

00:01:54.567 --> 00:01:56.968
Meanwhile, Russian and Chinese state media figures

00:01:56.968 --> 00:01:58.801
already asked Elon to stop identifying

00:01:58.801 --> 00:02:00.267
their accounts as propaganda.

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:02.901
It's always a good sign when Russia and China are like,

00:02:02.901 --> 00:02:05.534
"Finally, a guy we can work with."

00:02:05.534 --> 00:02:06.634
Some more business news --

00:02:06.634 --> 00:02:08.267
due than worse than expected earnings,

00:02:08.267 --> 00:02:11.434
I saw that Amazon is no longer a trillion-dollar company.

00:02:11.434 --> 00:02:13.167
And just from talking to Alexa,

00:02:13.167 --> 00:02:15.601
you can tell that Amazon is suddenly a little light on cash.

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:18.501
I'll show you what I mean. Alexa, what's the weather?

00:02:18.501 --> 00:02:21.000
-Alexa: Give me 20 bucks, and I'll tell you.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:24.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.367 --> 00:02:26.167
[ Applause ]

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:33.367
-Alexa, I'm not gonna give you 20 bucks.

00:02:33.367 --> 00:02:37.200
-Alexa: How about 10 bucks to bet on "FanDoo-el"?

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.501
-I'm not gonna do that. I think it's time for you to go.

00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:42.167
-Alexa: Whatever. Check me out on OnlyFans.

00:02:42.167 --> 00:02:44.234
-Ohh.

00:02:44.234 --> 00:02:46.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.267 --> 00:02:48.167
-Alexa...

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:51.267
-Guys, did you see that Senate Majority Leader Chuck Schumer

00:02:51.267 --> 00:02:53.868
was caught on a hot mic telling President Biden

00:02:53.868 --> 00:02:56.434
that Democrats are going downhill in Georgia

00:02:56.434 --> 00:02:59.567
as Herschel Walker climbs in the polls.

00:02:59.567 --> 00:03:01.167
Yeah, I'm actually not surprised

00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:02.834
Herschel Walker is climbing in the polls.

00:03:02.834 --> 00:03:04.968
He's somehow the most anti- and pro-abortion candidate

00:03:04.968 --> 00:03:06.534
of all time.

00:03:06.534 --> 00:03:08.534
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:11.434
-Come on! -Amazing.

00:03:11.434 --> 00:03:13.100
-That's a good joke! -Never seen anything like it.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:14.634
-Wow. -It's tough for Schumer.

00:03:14.634 --> 00:03:16.334
You got to try and talk soft enough

00:03:16.334 --> 00:03:17.701
so the mic doesn't pick you up

00:03:17.701 --> 00:03:20.067
but loud enough so Biden can hear.

00:03:20.067 --> 00:03:21.200
I don't blame him.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:23.133
Why don't we check in with Steve Mandel

00:03:23.133 --> 00:03:25.000
for some more bad Halloween advice. Steve?

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:26.667
-Be careful out there.

00:03:26.667 --> 00:03:29.567
Sometimes when you think you're buying edibles,

00:03:29.567 --> 00:03:32.234
they turn out to just be candy.

00:03:32.234 --> 00:03:34.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:40.267
-Well, listen to this. YouTube just announced

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:42.868
that doctors and nurses can now apply for their videos

00:03:42.868 --> 00:03:44.234
to be marked as "reliable."

00:03:44.234 --> 00:03:46.667
Well, if you're still unsure of what to believe,

00:03:46.667 --> 00:03:49.634
here are some helpful hints to tell whether a YouTube doctor

00:03:49.634 --> 00:03:51.334
is reliable or not.

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:53.601
For example, reliable ends videos with...

00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:02.634
Brah!

00:04:02.634 --> 00:04:05.133
Smash it, brah!

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:06.934
You see, here's another example.

00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:16.300
♪ Take me to the river ♪

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:18.434
♪ Drop me in the water ♪

00:04:18.434 --> 00:04:20.067
Next up...

00:04:20.133 --> 00:04:28.834
reliable, suggests pain meds through your general

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:31.067
"Talk to Kurt. Talk to Kurt."

00:04:31.067 --> 00:04:32.567
Reliable...

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:39.234
-Ooh.

00:04:39.234 --> 00:04:41.133
-Here's a final example.

00:04:45.634 --> 00:04:48.400
I hope those help. I hope that helps you out.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:50.067
Some sports news -- tonight was game one

